Story: Watching a game of tag by plan
  As a developer of a ground control agent
  I want to watch the scripted agent play tag with three real ArduPilot planes
  So that I have a baseline for my own agent

  The runner starts three ArduPlane SITL planes and plays a game of tag with them. The scripted
  ground control agent flies every plane by plan in AGENT mode. After the game, you send a plan
  of your own to the first plane, and you watch its status.

  Scenario: Play and watch
    When the planes play a game of tag
    Then the planes in AGENT mode are 3
    And the refused commands are 0
    And the reports of the hand-overs are complete
    When the ground sends a go-to plan
    Then the reply to the plan is accepted
    When the operator watches the status for 10 seconds
    Then the status reports in 10 seconds are between 9 and 11

Story: Sending your first plan
  As an operator of a plane in AGENT mode
  I want to send a plan and read the reply
  So that I know that the plane flies my plan

  You send a go-to plan from the console of the runner. The plane refuses it in FBWA, and it
  takes it in AGENT mode. Then you send a plan with an error, and a new plan. The reply and
  the status of the plane tell you what the plane does with each one.

  Scenario: Send a plan
    Given the flight mode of the plane is FBWA
    When the ground sends a go-to plan
    Then the reply to the plan is refused for the mode
    When the flight mode of the plane is AGENT
    Then the reported plan is 0
    When the ground sends a go-to plan
    Then the reply to the plan is accepted
    And the reported plan is 1
    And the reported primitive is go to
    When the ground sends a malformed plan
    Then the reply to the plan is refused as malformed
    And the reported plan is 1
    When the ground sends an orbit plan
    Then the reported plan is 2
    And the reported primitive is orbit

Story: Letting a plan run out
  As an operator of a plane in AGENT mode
  I want the plane to stay safe when the plans stop
  So that a lost link does not send the plane away

  Each plan is good only for its time to live. You send a plan that is good for 5 s, and you
  send nothing after it. The plane circles where it is and tells you why. A new plan ends the
  circle.

  Scenario: Let a plan run out
    When the ground sends a short go-to plan
    Then the reply to the plan is accepted
    When the plane flies on for 10 seconds
    Then the reported fallback is plan expired
    When the ground sends a go-to plan
    Then the reported fallback is none or recovery
    And the reported plan is 2
